# CI often executes from `main`

Many GitHub Actions and Jenkins setups load pipeline definitions from `main`
(or another tracked default branch). Edits on a feature branch or only in the
working tree have **no effect** until that branch sees them.

## Rule

When you change a CI workflow or pipeline definition:

- Commit related files together (workflow/Jenkinsfile plus scripts/config it
  drives) when the user asks to commit
- Remind the user that the change must reach the tracked branch (`main` /
  default) before runners will pick it up
- Do **not** commit or push automatically unless the consuming project has an
  explicit preference for that

## Scope

- GitHub Actions: `.github/workflows/**`
- Jenkins / custom pipelines: `Jenkinsfile`, `**/pipeline/*` entrypoints

## Why

SCM-driven CI checks out a specific branch; there may be no PR-preview path.
A pipeline change is “live” only once that branch has the commit.
